rca of the issue:
BUG: Language switcher click ignored when URL has ?lang= param.

REPRODUCTION:
1. Visit https://trending-news-3.preview.emergentagent.com/?lang=es (or any other lang in URL).
2. Click [data-testid='lang-switcher-button'] → menu opens.
3. Click [data-testid='lang-option-fr'].
4. EXPECTED: page reloads in French (Découvrez la vérité..., Accueil, FR badge).
5. ACTUAL: page reloads in Spanish — html.lang='es-ES', localStorage='es' (overwritten by useEffect), badge='ES', H1='Descubre la verdad...'.

ROOT CAUSE:
- /app/frontend/src/components/LanguageSwitcher.jsx:48-55 calls setLang(l.code) which writes localStorage='fr', then window.location.reload() reloads the SAME URL (still '?lang=es').
- /app/frontend/src/lib/i18n.js:103-114 detectInitial() reads URL '?lang=' FIRST (line 105-106), then localStorage. Since URL still says lang=es, initial state returns 'es'. Then useEffect line 169-174 writes localStorage='es' again, overwriting the 'fr' that was just set. Bug fully reproducible.

MITIGATION (one-line code fix in LanguageSwitcher.jsx line 49-54):
```jsx
onClick={() => {
  setLang(l.code);
  setOpen(false);
  if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {
    try {
      const u = new URL(window.location.href);
      u.searchParams.set('lang', l.code);
      window.history.replaceState({}, '', u.toString());
    } catch {}
    setTimeout(() => window.location.reload(), 80);
  }
}}
```

This keeps URL ?lang= in sync with the user's selection so detectInitial reads the correct value on reload. After fix: Playwright TEST 4 (switcher reload to FR from ES URL) and TEST 5 (footer renders in FR) should both pass. No backend changes needed.
